uctive amination pathway (2 steps)\n  - P4: Formamide\u2013aminoethanol\u2013aminoacetaldehyde route (4 steps)\n  - P5: Methanimine\u2013aminoacetonitrile Strecker variant (3 steps)\n  - P6: Photochemical HCN from CH4/NH3 \u2013 glycolonitrile Strecker (4 steps)\n  - P7: Surface-catalyzed formamide pathway (5 steps)\n  - P8: HCN\u2013methanimine Strecker\u2013glycine (4 steps)\n  - P9: Wet-dry cycling aminoacetaldehyde pathway (3 steps)\n  - P10: Hydrolysis of aminoacetonitrile from HCN-methanimine route (3 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 14 reactions | 1 balanced as written | 1 balanceable with coefficients | 10 UNBALANCED | 2 unchecked\n  - rxn_001 balanceable: CO2 + CH4 -> 2 HCHO\n  - rxn_002 UNBALANCED: CH4 + NH3 -> HCN | reactants minus products: H+6 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product\n  - rxn_004 UNBALANCED: HOCH2CN + NH3 -> NH2CH2CN | reactants minus products: H+2, O+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product\n  - rxn_005 UNBALANCED: NH2CH2CN -> NH2COOH | reactants minus products: H-1, N+1, O-2 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_006 UNBALANCED: HCN + HCHO -> NH2CHO | reactants minus products: C+1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_007 UNBALANCED: HCHO + NH3 -> NH2COOH | reactants minus products: C-1, O-1 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; CO as reactant\n  - rxn_008 UNBALANCED: CH3CN + NH3 -> NH2CH2CN | reactants minus products: H+2 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; HCN as reactant\n  - rxn_009 UNBALANCED: CH4 + HCN -> CH3CN | reactants minus products: H+2 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; NH3 as product\n  - rxn_010 UNBALANCED: NH2CHO + HCHO -> NH2CH2OH | reactants minus products: H