(Spontaneous formation of ammonium glycinate from aminoacetonitrile and water) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_018: mol_001, mol_005 -> mol_012, mol_004 (CO2 reduction to CO) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_019: mol_012, mol_002, mol_005 -> mol_015, mol_004 (CO amination to methanimine) [Hydrothermal]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Canonical Strecker synthesis from formaldehyde (4 steps)\n  - P2: Direct one-pot Strecker with UV (2 steps)\n  - P3: Hydrothermal Strecker variant (3 steps)\n  - P4: Ammonium glycinate hydrolysis (4 steps)\n  - P5: Hydroxyacetic acid route (4 steps)\n  - P6: Methylamine reductive carboxylation (2 steps)\n  - P7: Methanimine CO2 photocarboxylation (3 steps)\n  - P8: Ethanolamine carboxylation route (3 steps)\n  - P9: CO-reductive amination-methanimine route (3 steps)\n  - P10: Double hydrolysis and amination route (3 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 19 reactions | 9 balanced as written | 4 balanceable with coefficients | 6 UNBALANCED | 0 unchecked\n  - rxn_001 balanceable: CO2 + 2 H2 -> HCHO + H2O\n  - rxn_003 balanceable: CH4 + CO2 + 2 NH3 -> 2 HCN + 2 H2 + 2 H2O\n  - rxn_006 balanceable: NH2CH2CN + 2 H2O -> NH2CH2COOH + NH3\n  - rxn_007 UNBALANCED: HCHO + HCN + NH3 + H2O -> NH2CH2COOH | reactants minus products: H+3, N+1 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; NH3 as product; CO2 as reactant; CO as reactant\n  - rxn_008 UNBALANCED: CH3NH2 + CO2 -> NH2CH2COOH + H2 | reactants minus products: H-2 | balanceable if adding: H2 as reactant; HCN as product\n  - rxn_009 UNBALANCED: CH2NH + CO2 + H2O -> NH2CH2COOH | reactants minus products: O+1 | balanceable if adding: NH3 as product; O2 as product\n  - rxn_010 UNBALANCED: HCHO + HCN + NH3 + H2O -> NH2CH2COOH | reactants minus products: H+3,